<title>ARGENTINA: ARGENTINA AUCTIONS 182-, 91-DAY LETES T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>ARGENTINA AUCTIONS 182-, 91-DAY LETES T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina Tuesday auctioned $250 million in 182-day Letes Treasury bills at a cut-off yield of 5.70 percent and 250 million pesos of 91-day bills at 5.60 percent, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>There were 55 bids on the 182-day bills for a bid-to-cover ratio of 3.98 times and 55 bids for the 91-day bills for a bid-to-cover of 3.54 times.  </p>
<p>The price at the cut-off on the 182-day bills was 971.1833 and on the 91-day bills 985.8444.</p>
<p>Market-makers will be offered up to 10 percent more of both issues until 1700 local/2000 GMT.</p>
<p>Settlement is due August 15.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
